The sector picture was split: Canadian financials and gold miners rose; energy names fell 3.4% on the index as crude oil continued to pull back on Hormuz reopening expectations. The Canadian dollar softened slightly to 0.7236 against the US dollar.<br><br>
The other major development this week is Canadian bank earnings: BMO and Scotiabank report Wednesday, RBC, TD, and CIBC on Thursday, National Bank on Friday. Banks carry roughly 33% of the TSX''s weight. I will be in touch after the earnings picture is clearer.<br><br>
