The TSX gained 1.04% on Monday on Iran deal optimism. What the headline does not capture: US markets were closed for Memorial Day, so the move happened without Wall Street''s participation -- the first full North American session is today. The deal itself remains a framework, not a confirmed reopening, with the Hormuz still physically closed and approximately 240 ships awaiting passage.<br><br>
This week also brings Canadian bank earnings -- the sector that carries 33% of the TSX''s weight. BMO and Scotiabank report Wednesday; RBC, TD, and CIBC on Thursday. Those results, combined with how the US market responds to the Iran news on its first open day, will do more to determine the TSX''s direction this week than Monday''s session alone.<br><br>
If you are navigating this without a clear framework, I am happy to walk through the picture in a brief call.<br><br>
